# A type says what the number is, never how it is boxed: `case 3` makes x an int32 by type, and its word is still the box of a double. A list of int32s is read by the lower halves of its words: 0 was read for 3.
# The word of an operand goes into a list that may hold int32s through ElementAccessEmitter::storeWordOfOperand(), in every build: an int32 by type that goes as the word that it came in stops the build by name.
# THE LIE, testing=Int32sGoIntoListsInTheBoxesTheyCameIn: ArrayIntrinsicEmitter::putInBounds() leaves its conversion out.
